### A runnable request file (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client).
### The dev profile serves both the API and the flaky payment stub on the same port.
@host = http://localhost:8080

### --- payment stub control -------------------------------------------------
### ok | flaky | down | throttled | declined | slow
POST {{host}}/stub/payments/mode?value=ok

###
GET {{host}}/stub/payments/mode

### --- orders ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Place an order. 201 + Location; the charge happens after commit.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Actor: alice
X-Correlation-Id: demo-0001

{
  "customerEmail": "alice@example.com",
  "currency": "EUR",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "SKU-LAPTOP", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 999.99 },
    { "sku": "SKU-MOUSE", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 25.50 }
  ]
}

### Validation failure -> 400 application/problem+json with per-field errors.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "not-an-email", "currency": "eur", "lines": [] }

### Insufficient stock -> 409 with sku/requested/available extensions.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "greedy@example.com",
  "currency": "EUR",
  "lines": [{ "sku": "SKU-DOCK", "quantity": 999, "unitPrice": 5.00 }]
}

### Fetch one (note the ETag, derived from the @Version column).
GET {{host}}/api/orders/REPLACE_WITH_ORDER_NUMBER

### Search: paging, sorting, and the case-insensitive enum converter.
GET {{host}}/api/orders?status=paid&email=alice&page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc

### Aggregates: JPQL constructor expression + JdbcClient reporting query.
GET {{host}}/api/orders/statistics?days=30

### Cached read (Caffeine, 5 min TTL).
GET {{host}}/api/orders/customers/alice@example.com/lifetime-value

### Cancel - 409 unless the order is NEW or PAID.
POST {{host}}/api/orders/REPLACE_WITH_ORDER_NUMBER/cancellation

### --- transaction laboratory -----------------------------------------------
### Every propagation mode, called from no transaction.
GET {{host}}/api/tx/propagation

### REQUIRED joins the caller: both snapshots share one transaction name.
GET {{host}}/api/tx/required-joins-caller

### Scenarios. "rows" in the response shows what actually survived.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/requires-new-survives-rollback

### Savepoints over the JDBC transaction manager: outer commits, inner is discarded.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/nested-isolated

### The same thing under JpaTransactionManager: NestedTransactionNotSupportedException.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/nested-jpa-unsupported

### Swallowing an inner REQUIRED failure poisons the outer commit.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/required-poisons-outer

### A checked exception COMMITS by default.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/checked-commits

### ...unless you declare rollbackFor.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/checked-rolls-back

### this.method() bypasses the proxy: txName is the OUTER method.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/self-invocation-broken

### Through the injected proxy: txName is requiresNewInternal.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/self-invocation-fixed

### TransactionSynchronization callback order.
POST {{host}}/api/tx/scenarios/synchronization

### --- actuator -------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### Breaker state, reported without calling the dependency.
GET {{host}}/actuator/health/paymentGateway

### The custom @Endpoint from platform-starter.
GET {{host}}/actuator/platform

### A @Selector path variable.
GET {{host}}/actuator/platform/audit

### Reset the audit counters (@DeleteOperation).
DELETE {{host}}/actuator/platform

### Why is (or is not) a bean there?
GET {{host}}/actuator/conditions

### Every bound @ConfigurationProperties.
GET {{host}}/actuator/configprops

### Flyway migration history.
GET {{host}}/actuator/flyway

### Retry metrics.
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics/retry.attempts

### Prometheus scrape.
GET {{host}}/actuator/prometheus
